Subject: [PATCH] core: hold frame callbacks of surfaces not on screen

trynix carries this patch for wland's compositor until wland takes it.

tick fired every frame callback whose surface had committed since the
request, unless its window was minimized or hidden. A surface with
nothing on screen got its done too: one whose content went with an
attach(NULL), one whose xdg_toplevel was destroyed, one with no role.
weston and wlroots fire frame callbacks only for surfaces they paint,
so a callback of an unmapped surface waits until the surface is mapped
again or dies with it, and clients are written against that.

SDL 3 can lose track of a frame callback: in GZDoom's trace it asks
for two on a window's surface before the window's first frame and
keeps one, and the listener of the other points at the window's data.
When the window is hidden and destroyed, SDL detaches the surface's
buffer and commits, which latched that callback here, and the next
tick fired it into the freed window. GZDoom shows and destroys a window several
times while it picks a GL context. It crashed with SIGSEGV at a wild
address on each of four starts in a 928 px wide frame, and on each of
three second starts in a guest with a 753 px one.

A frame callback now fires only while its surface is shown
(surfaceShown, which presentation feedback already goes by). The frame
callback test runs on a mapped toplevel, and checks that a callback
waits while the window has no content and that one latched by the
detaching commit of a destroyed toplevel never fires.

